.TH SENTRY-V2 8 "2026-10-28" "Sentry-v2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sentry-v2 \- act safely on pressure, unit failures and SELinux denials
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentry-v2
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-policies
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B sentry-v2
.B \-\-check
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-policies
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B sentry-v2
.B \-\-rollback\-only
.br
.B sentry-v2
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentry-v2
is the daemon behind
.BR sentry-v2.service .
It reads cgroup v2 pressure (PSI), systemd unit failures from the journal and
SELinux denials from the audit stream, links each failure to the denials
around it, and writes one redacted JSON bundle per incident to the
configured sinks.
.PP
Policies can throttle or freeze a unit, or back up its files and reload it.
Every action is time-boxed and rolled back on expiry, on shutdown and after a
crash. Nothing is applied unless both
.B daemon.mode
and the policy's
.B mode
are
.BR enforce ;
the shipped configuration is dry-run.
.PP
You normally start it with
.BR systemctl ,
not by hand.
.B systemctl reload sentry-v2
sends SIGHUP, which re-reads the configuration and policies; an invalid one
is rejected and the old one stays live.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
The global configuration. Default:
.IR /etc/sentry-v2/sentry-v2.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-policies " DIR"
The policies directory. Every
.I *.toml
file in it is loaded. Default:
.IR /etc/sentry-v2/policies.d .
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the configuration and policies, list each policy with its effective
mode, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-rollback\-only
Undo the throttles and freezes a stopped daemon left active, then exit. The
unit runs this after every stop
.RB ( ExecStopPost= ),
so a daemon that was killed and can't restart doesn't leave a unit throttled
or frozen. Don't run it while the daemon is running.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown, a valid configuration with
.BR \-\-check ,
or everything put back with
.BR \-\-rollback\-only .
.TP
.B 1
A rollback failed under
.BR \-\-rollback\-only .
.TP
.B 2
The configuration is invalid, a sink secret can't be read, or the command
line was wrong.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sentry-v2/sentry-v2.toml
Global configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/sentry-v2/policies.d/
Policies, one or more per file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sentry-v2/
State: the action journal, held units, backups, and bundles from the file sink.
.TP
.I /run/sentry-v2/control.sock
The control socket that
.BR sentry-v2ctl (8)
talks to.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sentry-v2ctl (8),
.BR systemd.resource-control (5),
.BR ausearch (8),
.BR audit2allow (1)
.PP
The full guides, including the configuration and policy reference:
.UR https://github.com/jamesconwaydev/sentry-v2/tree/main/docs
the Sentry-v2 docs
.UE
